00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:00.834
Right now, you're

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:02.202
looking at the chilling new video

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:03.436
that we have of Stanislav

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:04.871
Rzhitsky jogging

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:06.506
just moments before he was gunned down.

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:07.941
So you just see him there running.

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:09.309
He's shot and killed multiple times.

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:10.210
Seconds later,

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:11.544
You can see a man in

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:13.213
what appears to be a white hat

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:14.347
trailing him.

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:16.249
Now, it appears that Eric, his killer,

00:00:16.249 --> 00:00:17.450
could have tracked his movements

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.485
using the popular

00:00:18.485 --> 00:00:20.920
running app called Strava.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.022
Now, we have obtained here

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:23.356
at OUTFRONT post of Eric

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:25.325
Skis, two prior runs

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:26.860
to this one where he was gunned down

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:29.229
and murdered from July 3rd and July 5th.

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:30.930
Five days before he was killed.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.198
And look at the map.

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:33.299
Look at the map. Identical.

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:35.502
He takes the same route every time.

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:38.071
And it was along that very same route,

00:00:38.505 --> 00:00:40.740
very risky was killed.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:41.875
Nick Paton Walsh is following

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:42.809
all of these developments

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:43.843
and is OUTFRONT tonight.

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:45.211
And Nick, let's begin

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:46.079
with the breaking news.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:47.047
This tape that we've obtained

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:48.314
of a Russian general

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:48.915
fired

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:51.051
for speaking out against Putin's war,

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:52.452
senior Russian general

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:53.853
on those crucial front lines

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:55.755
in the south along shop Burisma.

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:56.589
It's hard to overstate

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.725
how significant this development is.

00:00:58.725 --> 00:00:59.359
Yes, certainly.

00:00:59.359 --> 00:00:59.859
And you've got to put it

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:01.761
in the context of the last remarkable

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:03.663
three weeks inside Putin's military.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.432
We've just had the violent armed

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:07.133
rebellion, a mercenary group. Yes.

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:08.334
But essentially fueled

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:10.203
by very similar complaints

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:11.571
about essentially Russia

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:13.173
losing the artillery war

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:14.974
in key front lines, as Yvonne

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:16.309
Popov was making.

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:17.177
Except Popov,

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:19.312
a general, is speaking from inside

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:21.147
Russia's top brass again

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:22.449
about their misconduct

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:24.717
and poor execution of this war.

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.686
And he spoken out and he's lost his job

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:27.487
very fast.

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:27.887
Now, this,

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:30.223
I think, is another sign of disarray,

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:30.990
the disarray

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.559
which we saw spilling out

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:34.494
after the Viognier rebellion.

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:37.130
And it comes in a really odd 48 hours

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:39.165
for Russia's top brass, where we've seen

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:41.101
high profile assassinations

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:42.502
deep inside Russia,

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:44.671
key commanders killed by missile strikes,

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:46.406
and now this extraordinary dissent

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:47.907
from Popov. Here's what we know

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:51.478
for Russian generals,

00:01:51.478 --> 00:01:52.312
a home one

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:54.180
so distant from the front

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.116
is no longer safe here.

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:57.817
Former Russian submarine commander

00:01:57.817 --> 00:01:59.219
Stanislav Brzezinski

00:01:59.219 --> 00:02:02.255
runs his usual route at the usual time,

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:05.558
but with a new, unnoticed companion

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:06.993
on a bicycle.

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:09.262
Moments later, he was gunned down.

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:11.064
Ukrainian Defense

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:12.098
Intelligence said

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:13.700
they had nothing to do with it,

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.536
but they knew a lot about it, saying

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:17.470
he had been shot

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:18.338
seven times

00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:19.772
with a marker of pistol

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.774
and heavy rain meant no witnesses.

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:24.911
Brzezinski commanded a Russian submarine

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:27.347
accused of many attacks on civilians

00:02:27.347 --> 00:02:28.648
Ukraine, also said,

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:29.382
although his family

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:31.050
reportedly denied that,

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.318
Ukraine added later,

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:33.720
perhaps sarcastically,

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.955
that he had been killed by his own men

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:38.458
who refused to kill Ukrainian civilians.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:41.561
Russia was quick to respond

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:43.263
with their own propaganda,

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:44.964
claiming to have captured the gunman

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:45.698
within hours.

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:47.267
Video We can't verify

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:48.835
but it was a crude bit

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:49.235
to show

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:50.637
they are in control

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:52.772
of the fate of their top brass.

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:55.141
After nine weeks of chaos,

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:56.276
Russian media

00:02:56.276 --> 00:02:57.110
said the killing

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:59.312
hinged on a clumsy detail

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:00.780
that Brzezinski had made

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.182
his daily run public.

00:03:02.182 --> 00:03:03.883
On the running app Strava,

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:05.418
which has a long history

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:06.152
of accidentally

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:07.921
exposing the location of people

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:10.223
who don't want to be found revealing U.S.

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:12.058
military bases in Syria

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:14.427
and Yemen five years ago,

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:15.395
there are the dead

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:18.231
and also the missing News Wednesday, too,

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:19.199
about this key.

00:03:19.199 --> 00:03:21.534
Putin Lieutenant Sergei Rivkin

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:23.069
vanished

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:23.970
since he appeared

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:26.005
early in the armed Virginia rebellion.

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:28.575
To plead for it to stop vigorously.

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:31.611
A top Russian lawmaker claimed he was,

00:03:31.611 --> 00:03:33.713
quote, resting, whatever that means,

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:36.783
reconstituting the games,

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:39.552
thinking of events and holding notes.

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:42.121
One of the first proposals

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:45.024
for the staff is yet more mystery,

00:03:45.191 --> 00:03:46.626
adding to the bigger one.

00:03:46.626 --> 00:03:47.794
Where is Russia's

00:03:47.794 --> 00:03:49.862
most prominent military figure?

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:51.331
Wagner rebellion leader

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:53.266
Yevgeny Prigozhin.

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:55.301
Not seen since the weekend revolt

